-- title:
--   Fixed positive-intensity finite-cap cash prefix: original negative-mark compensated positive excess has vanishing mean
-- statement:
--   For each fixed original positive-intensity finite-cap cash prefix n, let M_k be the exact centred physical original negative-jump marked sum minus its original finite-clock compensator on the refining signed-mask grid. The expected positive part of F_n - w(x) - M_k vanishes as the refinement k increases. Preserve the original Lévy process, original right-dividend and singular cash, ruin jump, horizon T and inclusive finite cap. This is the substantive stochastic finite-variation Stieltjes/HJB residual needed by the bvb12 fixed-prefix ledger.
-- source:
--   Avram Palmowski Pistorius 2007 Proposition 4(i) and (5.13); source-exact Proved bvb_phys39 compensated marked count, p3_comp8 prefix L1; finite-variation chain rule with original discount and ruin clock.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_SpectrallyNegativeLevy
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_DividendStrategy
open Classical MeasureTheory Set Filter AvramDividend.Classical
